---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import HeroProduct from '../components/HeroProduct.astro';
import OrderReview from '../components/OrderReview.astro';
import DemoCTA from '../components/DemoCTA.astro';
import { steps, faqs } from '../data/product';
---
<Layout>
  <section class="hero hero-reference">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span></span> SELF-ORDERING KIOSK SOFTWARE · PHILIPPINES</div>
      <h1>Self-Ordering<br /><span>Made Easy</span><br />for Your Business.</h1>
      <p class="hero-description">Give customers the freedom to explore your menu, select their favorites, and review their orders—all from one touchscreen.</p>
      <p class="hero-positioning">For cafés, bakeries, restaurants & quick-service businesses.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/features/">Explore EZ Kyosk</a><a class="button" href="/contact/">Request a Demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="hero-footnote">Your Menu. Their Order. One Simple Screen.</div>
    </div>
    <HeroProduct />
  </section>

  <section class="industry-strip" aria-label="Designed for food and beverage businesses">
    <span>YOUR MENU. THEIR ORDER. ONE SIMPLE SCREEN.</span>
    <div>Cafés <i aria-hidden="true">/</i> Bakeries <i aria-hidden="true">/</i> Restaurants <i aria-hidden="true">/</i> Quick-service</div>
  </section>

  <section class="intro section">
    <div><div class="eyebrow">A BETTER WAY TO TAKE ORDERS</div><h2>Let customers handle<br />the ordering.<br /><em>Let your team handle<br />the service.</em></h2></div>
    <div class="intro-text"><p class="large-copy">A dedicated screen for ordering.<br />More attention for hospitality.</p><p>Let customers browse the menu, make their selections, and review their orders at their own pace. Give guests another way to order while staff focus on food preparation and customer service.</p><a class="text-link" href="/features/">Get to know the product <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="benefits section">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">WHY CONSIDER SELF-ORDERING?</div><h2>Clear choices for guests.<br />A considered tool for your team.</h2></div><p>A customer-facing ordering experience, built around the way food and beverage businesses serve.</p></div>
    <div class="three-columns">
      <article><span class="feature-icon">01 / DISCOVERY</span><h3>A menu worth exploring</h3><p>Give every category a place on screen, so customers can discover what you offer before deciding.</p></article>
      <article><span class="feature-icon">02 / CONTROL</span><h3>Orders at their own pace</h3><p>Customers can choose items, adjust quantities, and check their selection before confirming.</p></article>
      <article><span class="feature-icon">03 / CLARITY</span><h3>A clearer review step</h3><p>Bring the cart and calculated total together in one view, ready for a final check.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-section section">
    <OrderReview />
    <div><div class="eyebrow">THE CORE EXPERIENCE</div><h2>Everything customers need<br />to start an order.</h2><div class="feature-list">
      <div><span class="feature-number">01</span><div><h3>A digital menu, organized</h3><p>Browse products by category on a touchscreen.</p></div></div>
      <div><span class="feature-number">02</span><div><h3>A cart they can manage</h3><p>Add products and adjust quantities before moving on.</p></div></div>
      <div><span class="feature-number">03</span><div><h3>Review, then confirm</h3><p>See calculated totals and proceed to order confirmation.</p></div></div>
    </div><a class="text-link" href="/features/" style="margin-top:20px">Explore all features <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="workflow section">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">HOW EZ KYOSK WORKS</div><h2>Five simple steps.<br />One straightforward experience.</h2></div><p>From the first look at the menu to order confirmation, the next step stays clear.</p></div>
    <ol class="steps">{steps.map(([title, body], i) => <li><div class="step-number">0{i + 1}<span aria-hidden="true">→</span></div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{body}</p></li>)}</ol>
    <a class="text-link" href="/how-it-works/">Walk through the ordering flow <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </section>

  <section class="solutions-preview section">
    <div><div class="eyebrow">BUILT AROUND YOUR BUSINESS</div><h2>Different menus.<br /><em>One simple screen.</em></h2><p style="margin-top:24px">From a neighborhood bakery to a quick-service counter, explore how self-ordering could fit your place.</p></div>
    <div class="industry-list"><a href="/solutions/#cafes">Cafés & coffee shops <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/solutions/#bakeries">Bakeries & pastry shops <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/solutions/#restaurants">Restaurants <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/solutions/#quick-service">Quick-service businesses <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </section>

  <section id="integrations" class="roadmap section">
    <div><div class="eyebrow">DEVELOPMENT ROADMAP</div><h2>One kiosk today.<br />More possibilities ahead.</h2></div>
    <div><p>Menu browsing, categories, cart management, quantity adjustment, calculated totals, and order confirmation form the current product experience.</p><div class="integration-tags"><span>POS connections</span><span>Payment gateways</span><span>Receipt printing</span><span>Kitchen orders</span></div><p><strong>These integrations are planned.</strong> They are not confirmed production capabilities.</p><a class="text-link" href="/features/#planned">Understand the roadmap <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq section">
    <div class="faq-intro"><div class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU GET STARTED</div><h2>Good questions.<br /><em>Clear answers.</em></h2><p>What the software does, where it is heading, and what to discuss with us.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Have another question? <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    <div class="faq-list">{faqs.map(([question, answer]) => <details><summary>{question}<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>{answer}</p></details>)}</div>
  </section>
  <DemoCTA />
</Layout>
